d tree with crown height noticeably greater than crown width in the left leafed view, and closer to roughly equal height and width in the right leafed view; both read as tall, heavy, broad-domed specimens.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "foliage-to-low-skirt", "priority": "core", "observation": "Foliage-bearing branches descend very low on the trunk, with the lowest limbs sweeping outward and downward to near ground level and shading the turf beneath; only a short length of clear bole is exposed below the skirt.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "branch-layered-horizontal-tiers", "priority": "core", "observation": "Lateral limbs leave the trunk at wide angles and run outward in near-horizontal tiers, the tier tips arching slightly downward; this produces visible stacked layers of foliage within the crown mass and a strongly horizontal texture along the crown edges.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "bole-short-with-basal-flare", "priority": "core", "observation": "The bole is stout and comparatively short before dividing into several large ascending scaffold limbs; at ground level it widens into a smooth buttressed flare with broad low root swellings spreading into the lawn.", "reference_ids": ["reference-0", "reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "winter-fine-twiggy-periphery", "priority": "core", "observation": "In the leafless view the crown periphery is a fine, dense haze of very slender twigs, markedly finer than the scaffold limbs, producing a soft grey-brown cloud outline rather than a coarse open framework.", "reference_ids": ["reference-1"], "uncertain": false}, {"id": "winter-branch-hierarchy", "priority": "secondary", "observation": "Bare silhouette shows a clear size hierarchy: a few heavy ascending scaffold limbs from the low bole, dividing repeatedly into progressively thinner sub-branches, with lower limbs angled outward and near-horizontal